---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Contribute"
  description="Help preserve Catholic knowledge for humans and AI — an open-source project grounded in human agency."
>
  <section class="section-tight shell fade-in">
    <p class="eyebrow">✦ Contribute</p>
    <h1 class="h1">Work with us in the open.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Catholic Context is an open-source project. We build tools for AI and keep the human
      person at the center — so we can enable technology while preserving meaningful agency,
      and steward together the Church’s teaching as a shared inheritance.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell prose">
    <h2 class="h2">Why contribute</h2>
    <p>
      The greatest collection of knowledge in the world deserves careful hands. Contribution
      here is human stewardship: clarify wording, strengthen sources, surface problems, and
      help software stay faithful without replacing conscience or judgment.
    </p>
    <p>
      Principles from <em>Magnifica Humanitas</em> guide how Catholic-grounded AI should
      behave — especially the duty to preserve human dignity and agency. Read them in the
      <a href="/harness#humanitas-heading">Harness</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h2">Ways to help</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Propose corrections with sources on any knowledge page</li>
      <li>Improve citations, summaries, and classifications</li>
      <li>Suggest new knowledge objects that belong in the collection</li>
      <li>Strengthen Harness principles and public Evals</li>
      <li>Build applications on the open foundation</li>
      <li>Review documentation and schemas for clarity</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h2">How change becomes canonical</h2>
    <p>
      Anyone may inspect, fork, and propose. Merges remain reviewed. Theological material
      may require qualified review. Votes and popularity never decide doctrine — sources
      and responsible human judgment do.
    </p>

    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/knowledge">Start from Knowledge →</a>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href={SITE.githubUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
        View repository ↗
      </a>
      <a
        class="btn btn-secondary"
        href={`${SITE.githubUrl}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        target="_blank"
      >
        Contributing guide ↗
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
